{
  "id": "murphy-shakti8-limbic-workout-temporal",
  "name": "8 Coil Shakti: Limbic Workout (temporal)",
  "category": "signals",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "fidelity": "approximation",
  "dose": {"value": [10, 50], "unit": "mG", "plane": "unstated", "cite": "Murphy, measurement.htm"},
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti software); signal templates licensed from Persinger & Koren",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Todd Murphy's 'Limbic Workout' (descending lability batch) for the 8 Coil Shakti: seven 5-min signals (chirp, caudate, Fibonacci, slow and standard hippocampus, short-latency and standard amygdala) with 90-s silences, over both temporal lobes. All seven waveforms are stand-ins. Murphy states that the brain gets 'a novel stimulation every few minutes' and so avoids habituation.",
  "notes": "The vendor: 'It uses seven signals. There is a 90 second silent gap between each phase, for a total of 13 phases.' (descending_lability_batch_consent.htm); each signal runs 5 min. This helmet allows 12 phases: the silence between the slow and the standard hippocampal signal is left out (42.5 min instead of 44). All eight coils run together on the cross over each temporal lobe (site names: this project's reading); C5, FT7, T10 and TP8 are reversed, after the vendor's coil chart. All seven are stand-ins. Chirp: a 40 to 6 Hz sweep, 837 points of 3 ms (the Thomas pattern's length, Dixon 2001 p.4 [90]), unlike the vendor's description (mod40_chirp_consent.htm). Caudate (a rising sweep over 1.5 s) and Fibonacci (100 Hz bursts at 5 Hz with Fibonacci strengths) have no description to build from. Hippocampus: the primed burst, one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]); the slow form uses 4-ms points. Amygdala: the project's rising sweep with the published point duration and length (230 points of 3 ms; Ryczko 2002 p.1 [592]); its point values were never published as numbers. 'Shorter latency' repeats every 3 s (Ryczko 2002 p.2 [593]); the vendor gives no value. The vendor's 10 to 50 mG carries no distance (measurement.htm, duds.htm); an independent meter read 0.1 to 1.0 uT RMS about 9 cm from the coils (Gendle 2012 p.11 [227]). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. The effects are vendor claims. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). If headache or pressure appears, lower the intensity by one third. Not for anyone with epilepsy, a psychiatric condition or medication, migraine or brain injury, or on drugs. Stop on fear or distress.",
  "setting": "The vendor's session takes about 45 min (42.5 min here). Darkness and silence for effects during the session; eyes closed, relaxed without meditating or falling asleep. Bilateral placement only.",
  "schedule": "Vendor's general Shakti rules: at most every 72 h or once a week, never on consecutive days; a series of 3 or 6 sessions, then a 21-day break.",
  "targets": ["caudate-nucleus", "left-hippocampus-head", "left-hippocampus-body", "left-hippocampus-tail", "right-hippocampus-head", "right-hippocampus-body", "right-hippocampus-tail", "left-amygdala", "right-amygdala", "left-temporal-pole", "left-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior", "right-temporal-pole", "right-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior"],
  "source": "Murphy, Shakti demo: Limbic Workout session https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/descending_lability_batch_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Limbic Workout output page https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/output_descending_lability_batch.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: 8-coil hippocampal signal (slow hippocampal file codes) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/8_coil_ltp_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Getting Started (8-coil chart, +/- coil pairs) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/getting_started_basic.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Caudate nucleus signal https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/caudate_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Fibonacci and hippocampus session https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/fibb_hipp_bat_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Amygdala (left) and hippocampus (right) signals (alternative 'slow' hippocampal signal) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/amy_l_hipp_r_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Modulated 40 Hz chirp signal https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/mod40_chirp_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: What are 'Rapid' and 'High-Speed' signals? (3-ms points, 4-s latency) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Formal Discussion (about 9.6 s of field per minute, 10-20 mG) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/mono_proposal.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Random Theta Band output (LTP spectral peak 5.4 Hz) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/5jut4ranconsent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Safety - how often https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/how_often_is_safe.htm ; Ryczko & Persinger 2002, Percept Mot Skills 95:592 (230-point burst-firing pattern once every 3 s) https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12434855/ ; Dixon & Persinger 2001, Int J Neurosci 108:8